**Before:** The raw adjacency list `ArrayList<ArrayList<Integer>>` was passed directly into `dfs` and `dfsRec`, and `addEdge` lived on the search class itself.

**After:**

1. **`GraphInterface`** — an interface the algorithm depends on, with `getNeighbors(int)` and `size()`. Any graph representation can implement it.
2. **`Graph`** — wraps the original adjacency list and implements `GraphInterface`. `addEdge` moved here where it belongs.
3. **`DepthFirstSearch.dfs` / `dfsRec`** — now accept `GraphInterface` instead of `ArrayList<ArrayList<Integer>>`. The algorithm has no knowledge of the underlying data structure.

The search algorithm can now work with any graph (adjacency matrix, database-backed, etc.) without modification — just implement `GraphInterface`.

